#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:5
#: 5e2963a12ad846b89b1fca3a83aa1a07
msgid "Surface Tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:7
#: 8171d8e498d243bb8922fe99b9085af7
msgid "Copter supports low altitude Surface Tracking, either a floor/ground or a ceiling, in nearly all modes including pilot controlled modes like :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>`, :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>` and :ref:`PosHold <poshold-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:9
#: 142b39cbde0d4ea985e298027d2a3c22
msgid "Additionally, :ref:`Terrain Following<terrain-following>` is supported in autonomous modes using a terrain height data base stored on the autopilot's SD card and/or obtained real-time from the Ground Control Station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:11
#: c98572e53bf84db7b74de307fa503ff1
msgid "This page describes the Surface Following setup .  For autonomous modes using downloaded data for Terrain Following please see the :ref:`terrain following for autonomous modes <terrain-following>` wiki page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:17
#: 21dd70f4777b4cceb1499eeeb902a14f
msgid "Setup and Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:19
#: 175e3ad432aa4f26a630c7b781d10a14
msgid "Connect a downward facing rangefinder(for floor/ground tracking) and/or an upward facing rangefinder (for ceiling tracking) :ref:`lidar or sonar <common-rangefinder-landingpage>` to the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:21
#: 05f54153b00349e89d4f0b28437e33c6
msgid "Which is being used is configured by the :ref:`SURFTRAK_MODE<SURFTRAK_MODE>` parameter or by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:22
#: fc66e9b4720e4a78aca2f6c2739cb775
msgid "An :ref:`auxiliary switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` (function \"75\"), or  :ref:`channel-7-and-8-options`, can be configured to turn on/off use of the rangefinder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:23
#: 930e6d9ed3ec4c1f850a7810f068caa9
msgid "the :ref:`SURFTRAK_TC<SURFTRAK_TC>` parameter controls the smoothing of the surface data. Increase if you are moving fast and getting perturbations in the flight path. Conversely, it can be lower to make the vehicle more responsive to the rangefinder data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:27
#: 6534543997ed46bfa82086b6b421c853
msgid "Do not set the :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ <EK3_SRC1_POSZ>` to Rangefinder.  This parameter should be left at the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:29
#: 1a46fc5b1c794f0a956eb1e544d602a6
msgid "Do not set :ref:`EK3_RNG_USE_HGT <EK3_RNG_USE_HGT>` parameter.  This parameter should be left at \"-1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:32
#: 0a1e0501edcb4967800d51a1d5549d7e
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:34
#: d497c1c361734a0080512d6ff4e2bda6
msgid "When the rangefinder can \"see\" the ground, the pilot's throttle stick adjusts the target altitude above the ground (i.e. the attitude corrected distance from the range finder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/terrain-following-manual-modes.rst:35
#: 5429d6f5ec5f4e27adf8a9d1f84cb007
msgid "When the vehicle climbs out of the rangefinder's range the pilot's stick returns to directly controlling the vehicle's target climb rate (i.e. EKF estimated climb rate based on barometer and accelerometer).  When the vehicle comes back within the range of the ground, the target altitude above the terrain is reset to the current altitude above terrain. For more information, see :ref:`Understanding Altitude in ArduPilot <common-understanding-altitude>`."
msgstr ""
